content.text:
```css
&::after {
  content: "• You are\A here";
  white-space: pre-line;
}
```

Measured: 19px (one line) without a `white-space` change, 38px (two lines) with it. Works on the pseudo-element or inherited from the parent.

`pre-line` is usually the one you want — honors the `\A` but still collapses your other whitespace and wraps normally. `pre` and `pre-wrap` also work but stop collapsing spaces.

Watch the space after `\A`: the escape eats one following whitespace char as a delimiter, so `"a\A b"` gives you `a` / `b`, not `a` / ` b`.

